    "summary": "Flat piece of wood pierced with two slits and painted on one side dark blue and red. Convex edge is pierced with holes to which is attached a fringe of large brown seed or nut shells painted red. Along the straighter edge are holes for pegs, one of which still remains. Small tuft of cassowary feathers at one end. Wood appears to be pine. (Register description)",
